From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:03:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: Forget the SDOUT idle configuration when
 resetting the chip

tas2764_set_dai_tdm_idle() skips the register writes when the requested
idle mask and mode match idle_slot_config. That cache lives in the I2C
driver data, but tas2764_codec_probe() resets the chip, which puts the
SDOUT idle slots back to Hi-Z, every time the component is probed. When
the sound card is bound again before tas2764_set_bclk_ratio() has
cropped the cached mask, for example after a probe deferral, the same
configuration is requested again and never written, and the unused
slots stay Hi-Z.

Clear the cached configuration together with the register cache after
the reset.

Fixes: 45573ee1f2ba ("ASoC: tas2764: expose SDOUT bus keeper via set_tdm_idle operation")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index e876702..52b15cf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -784,6 +784,9 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 
 	tas2764_reset(tas2764);
 	regmap_reinit_cache(tas2764->regmap, &tas2764_i2c_regmap);
+	/* The reset put the SDOUT idle slots back to Hi-Z */
+	tas2764->idle_slot_config.tx_mask = 0;
+	tas2764->idle_slot_config.tx_mode = 0;
 
 	if (tas2764->irq) {
 		ret = snd_soc_component_write(tas2764->component, TAS2764_INT_MASK0, 0x00);
